  "findings": [
    {
      "cases": [
        "A3",
        "A3b",
        "A4",
        "A4b"
      ],
      "result": "The authoritative transaction compares the epoch before replay and resolves a current request through its scoped binding and eligible linked job. Fresh bindings never reuse a normalized-text match, including a same-scope/current job with another binding. Seeded historical, legacy, other-scope and unrelated-binding controls exercise the prior reuse gap. Current payload or consent changes conflict, expired ones stay stale, and incompatible links return unavailable without repair or disclosure."
    },
    {
      "cases": [
        "A5",
        "A5b",
        "A5c"
      ],
      "result": "The trust boundary now binds the exact decoded original, server analysis and extracted effect to the same epoch/import, route policy and engine/index. Whole-request literals are withheld before fallback. Extracted-only literals create no C013 candidate evidence or effect. The unrelated-effects rule preserves ordinary eligibility, and mismatch checks each have a coherent positive control. Synthetic identity does not establish production invocation authority."
    },
    {
      "cases": [
        "A7a",
        "A7b"
      ],
      "result": "The disposable result store puts validation and the publishable write in one authoritative operation. The projection validates authority and reads the saved payload together. Separate immediate and partial save tests exercise pre-save revocation. Immediate-response and saved-progress reads exercise pre-disclosure revocation. Retained historical state remains distinct from current disclosure and intake is not repeated."
    },
    {
      "cases": [
        "A1",
        "A2",
        "A6"
      ],
      "result": "Same-import epoch advance still returns stale before admission. A2 now expressly uses valid consent and a valid token with missing authority. A6 preserves failure after job creation and verifies rollback of the committed state in both tables."
    }
  ],
  "implementation_review_checks": [
    "Add a mismatched binding-identity variant to A4b even when scope and epoch match, since v2 requires all three fields to agree.",
    "Add a mixed-input control with a protected fragment and an unrelated eligible effect. Require suppression of only the protected effect and a single properly bound job for the unrelated effect.",
    "For A7a, compare old publishable state before and after a stale attempted update as well as testing a fresh result. Exercise the epoch checks in the actual disposable Convex operations, and record any limits of the harness when exercising transaction conflicts."
  ],
